speechtext:
On the point of order,
Mr. Chairman. What I said before I maintain still. I said nothing about whether the minister would or would not answer. I declared it was the right of any hon. member to_ address the committee when no one else had the floor. The point of order raised by [Mr. F. R. MacMillan.}
the hon. member for Vancouver Centre (Mr. Mackenzie) was that my friend from Saskatoon (Mr. MacMillan), had no right to speak-
